@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Optional in Java";
}

<div class="card border-0 shadow-sm">
    <div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">

        <!-- HEADER -->
        <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">Optional in Java</h2>

            <p class="lead text-muted mb-0">
                Learn how Java's Optional class represents a value that may or
                may not be present, helping developers write clearer code for
                potentially missing values.
            </p>
        </div>


        <!-- INTRODUCTION -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">What is Optional?</h3>

            <p>
                <code>Optional&lt;T&gt;</code> is a container object that may
                contain a non-null value or may be empty.
            </p>

            <p>
                It is commonly used as a return type when the absence of a
                result is a valid possibility.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Concept</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>
                                            Value Available
                                                  ↓
                                            Optional&lt;T&gt;
                                                  ↓
                                                Use Value
                                                  ↓
                                                No Value
                                                  ↓
                                            Optional.empty()
                                                  ↓
                                            Handle Absence</code></pre>                   
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- CREATING OPTIONAL -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Creating Optional
            </h3>

            <p>
                Java provides several factory methods for creating Optional
                instances.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; value =
    Optional.of("CIIT");

Optional&lt;String&gt; empty =
    Optional.empty();

Optional&lt;String&gt; nullable =
    Optional.ofNullable(
        getName()
    );</code></pre>
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- OF -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Optional.of()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>Optional.of()</code> creates an Optional containing a
                non-null value.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.of("Sam");

System.out.println(name);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional[Sam]</code></pre>
</div>

            <div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
                <strong>Important:</strong>
                Passing <code>null</code> to <code>Optional.of()</code> throws
                <code>NullPointerException</code>.
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- OF NULLABLE -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Optional.ofNullable()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>Optional.ofNullable()</code> creates an Optional that
                contains the value when it is non-null, otherwise it creates
                an empty Optional.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>String name = null;

Optional&lt;String&gt; result =
    Optional.ofNullable(name);

System.out.println(result);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional.empty</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- EMPTY -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Optional.empty()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>Optional.empty()</code> represents an Optional with no
                value.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; result =
    Optional.empty();

System.out.println(
    result.isEmpty()
);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>true</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- ISPRESENT -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                isPresent()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>isPresent()</code> checks whether a value exists.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.of("Neha");

if (name.isPresent()) {

    System.out.println(
        "Value is available"
    );

}</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>Value is available</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- ISEMPTY -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                isEmpty()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>isEmpty()</code> checks whether an Optional contains no
                value.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.empty();

if (name.isEmpty()) {

    System.out.println(
        "No value available"
    );

}</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>No value available</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- GET -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                get()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>get()</code> returns the contained value.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.of("Sam");

String value =
    name.get();

System.out.println(value);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>Sam</code></pre>
</div>

            <div class="alert alert-danger mt-3">
                Avoid calling <code>get()</code> blindly. If the Optional is
                empty, <code>get()</code> throws
                <code>NoSuchElementException</code>.
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- OR ELSE -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                orElse()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>orElse()</code> returns the contained value or a
                fallback value when the Optional is empty.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.empty();

String result =
    name.orElse("Unknown");

System.out.println(result);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>Unknown</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- OR ELSE GET -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                orElseGet()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>orElseGet()</code> accepts a Supplier and computes the
                fallback value when it is actually needed.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.empty();

String result =
    name.orElseGet(
        () -&gt; "Generated Name"
    );

System.out.println(result);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>Generated Name</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- OR ELSE THROW -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                orElseThrow()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>orElseThrow()</code> returns the value when present and
                throws an exception when the Optional is empty.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.of("Amit");

String result =
    name.orElseThrow();

System.out.println(result);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>Amit</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- CUSTOM EXCEPTION -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                orElseThrow() with Custom Exception
            </h3>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.empty();

String result =
    name.orElseThrow(
        () -&gt;
            new IllegalArgumentException(
                "Name not found"
            )
    );</code></pre>
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- IF PRESENT -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                ifPresent()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>ifPresent()</code> executes a Consumer when a value is
                present.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.of("Priya");

name.ifPresent(
    value -&gt;
        System.out.println(value)
);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>Priya</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- IF PRESENT OR ELSE -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                ifPresentOrElse()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>ifPresentOrElse()</code> allows separate actions for
                present and empty cases.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.ofNullable(
        getName()
    );

name.ifPresentOrElse(

    value -&gt;
        System.out.println(
            "Name: " + value
        ),

    () -&gt;
        System.out.println(
            "Name not found"
        )
);</code></pre>
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- FILTER -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                filter()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>filter()</code> keeps the Optional value only when it
                satisfies the supplied predicate.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;Integer&gt; age =
    Optional.of(25);

Optional&lt;Integer&gt; adultAge =
    age.filter(
        value -&gt; value &gt;= 18
    );

adultAge.ifPresent(
    System.out::println
);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>25</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- MAP -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                map()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>map()</code> transforms the value inside the Optional
                when it is present.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.of("java");

Optional&lt;String&gt; upper =
    name.map(
        String::toUpperCase
    );

System.out.println(
    upper.orElse("UNKNOWN")
);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>JAVA</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- FLATMAP -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                flatMap()
            </h3>

            <p>
                <code>flatMap()</code> is useful when the mapping function
                itself returns an Optional and you want to avoid nested
                Optional values.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; name =
    Optional.of("Amit");

Optional&lt;String&gt; result =
    name.flatMap(
        value -&gt;
            Optional.of(
                value.toUpperCase()
            )
    );

System.out.println(
    result.orElse("Unknown")
);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>AMIT</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- MAP VS FLATMAP -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                map() vs flatMap()
            </h3>

            <div class="table-responsive">

                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Operation</th>
                            <th>Use</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>

                    <tbody>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>map()</code></td>
                            <td>
                                Transforms the contained value.
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>flatMap()</code></td>
                            <td>
                                Transforms using a function that already
                                returns Optional and avoids nesting.
                            </td>
                        </tr>

                    </tbody>

                </table>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- OR -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                or()
            </h3>

            <p>
                The <code>or()</code> method can provide another Optional when
                the current Optional is empty.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;String&gt; primary =
    Optional.empty();

Optional&lt;String&gt; backup =
    Optional.of("Backup Value");

Optional&lt;String&gt; result =
    primary.or(
        () -&gt; backup
    );

System.out.println(
    result.orElse("None")
);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>Backup Value</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- STREAM -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Optional and Stream API
            </h3>

            <p>
                Optional integrates naturally with stream operations such as
                <code>findFirst()</code> and <code>findAny()</code>.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>List&lt;String&gt; names =
    List.of(
        "Amit",
        "Neha",
        "Rahul"
    );

Optional&lt;String&gt; result =
    names.stream()
        .filter(
            name -&gt;
                name.startsWith("N")
        )
        .findFirst();

result.ifPresent(
    System.out::println
);</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>Neha</code></pre>
</div>
        </section>


        <!-- RETURN TYPE -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Optional as a Method Return Type
            </h3>

            <p>
                One common use of Optional is representing a method result
                that may not exist.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;User&gt; findUserById(
    int id
) {

    // Search user

    return Optional.empty();
}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <p class="mt-3">
                The caller can explicitly handle the possibility that no user
                was found.
            </p>

        </section>


        <!-- REAL WORLD -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Real-World Example
            </h3>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>Optional&lt;User&gt; user =
    findUserById(101);

String name =
    user.map(
        User::getName
    )
    .orElse(
        "User Not Found"
    );

System.out.println(name);</code></pre>
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- OPTIONAL PRIMITIVES -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                OptionalInt, OptionalLong and OptionalDouble
            </h3>

            <p>
                Java provides primitive-specialized Optional classes for
                numeric values.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>OptionalInt age =
    OptionalInt.of(25);

if (age.isPresent()) {

    System.out.println(
        age.getAsInt()
    );

}</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3">
    Output:
</p>

<div class="code-block mb-4 shadow-sm">
    <div class="code-lang-tag">
        Output
    </div>

    <pre class="mb-0"><code>25</code></pre>
</div>

            <div class="table-responsive mt-3">

                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                    <thead class="table-dark">

                        <tr>
                            <th>Class</th>
                            <th>Value Type</th>
                        </tr>

                    </thead>

                    <tbody>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>Optional&lt;T&gt;</code></td>
                            <td>Reference type</td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>OptionalInt</code></td>
                            <td>int</td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>OptionalLong</code></td>
                            <td>long</td>
                        </tr>

                        <tr>
                            <td><code>OptionalDouble</code></td>
                            <td>double</td>
                        </tr>

                    </tbody>

                </table>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- BEST PRACTICES -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Optional Best Practices
            </h3>

            <ul>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Use Optional mainly as a return type where absence is
                    meaningful.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Avoid blindly calling <code>get()</code>.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Prefer <code>orElse()</code>,
                    <code>orElseGet()</code>, or
                    <code>orElseThrow()</code> when appropriate.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Use <code>map()</code> and <code>flatMap()</code> for
                    transformations.
                </li>

                <li class="mb-2">
                    Use <code>ifPresent()</code> when an action should happen
                    only when a value exists.
                </li>

                <li>
                    Do not use Optional merely to wrap every field in a domain
                    object.
                </li>

            </ul>

        </section>


        <!-- COMMON MISTAKES -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Common Mistakes
            </h3>

            <div class="alert alert-warning">

                <ul class="mb-0">

                    <li class="mb-2">
                        Calling <code>get()</code> without checking presence.
                    </li>

                    <li class="mb-2">
                        Using Optional everywhere instead of where it provides
                        meaningful semantics.
                    </li>

                    <li class="mb-2">
                        Returning <code>null</code> from a method declared to
                        return Optional.
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        Confusing <code>orElse()</code> with
                        <code>orElseGet()</code>.
                    </li>

                </ul>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- OR ELSE DIFFERENCE -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                orElse() vs orElseGet()
            </h3>

            <p>
                The fallback expression passed to <code>orElse()</code> is
                evaluated even when the Optional contains a value. With
                <code>orElseGet()</code>, the Supplier is invoked only when
                the Optional is empty.
            </p>

            <div class="code-block">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>String result =
    optionalValue.orElse(
        createDefaultValue()
    );</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="code-block mt-3">
                <div class="code-lang-tag">Java</div>

                <pre class="mb-0"><code>String result =
    optionalValue.orElseGet(
        () -&gt;
            createDefaultValue()
    );</code></pre>
            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- INTERVIEW -->
        <section class="mb-5">

            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Interview Questions
            </h3>

            <div class="accordion" id="optionalQuestions">

                <!-- Q1 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

