                <!-- Q2 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#optionalQuestionTwo">

                            What is the difference between of() and ofNullable()?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="optionalQuestionTwo"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#optionalQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            <code>of()</code> requires a non-null value and
                            throws NullPointerException for null.
                            <code>ofNullable()</code> creates an empty
                            Optional when the supplied value is null.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q3 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#optionalQuestionThree">

                            What is the difference between get() and orElse()?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="optionalQuestionThree"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#optionalQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            <code>get()</code> throws an exception when the
                            Optional is empty, while <code>orElse()</code>
                            returns a fallback value.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q4 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#optionalQuestionFour">

                            What is orElseGet()?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="optionalQuestionFour"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#optionalQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            <code>orElseGet()</code> accepts a Supplier and
                            calculates the fallback value only when the
                            Optional is empty.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q5 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#optionalQuestionFive">

                            What is the purpose of map() in Optional?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="optionalQuestionFive"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#optionalQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            <code>map()</code> transforms the contained value
                            when the Optional is present.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q6 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#optionalQuestionSix">

                            Why should get() be avoided when possible?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="optionalQuestionSix"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#optionalQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            Calling <code>get()</code> on an empty Optional
                            throws NoSuchElementException. Explicit fallback
                            or exception-handling methods are usually clearer.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>


                <!-- Q7 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">

                    <h2 class="accordion-header">

                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
                                type="button"
                                data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                                data-bs-target="#optionalQuestionSeven">

                            Can Optional contain null?

                        </button>

                    </h2>

                    <div id="optionalQuestionSeven"
                         class="accordion-collapse collapse"
                         data-bs-parent="#optionalQuestions">

                        <div class="accordion-body">

                            No. Optional itself represents either a non-null
                            value or absence. <code>Optional.of(null)</code>
                            throws an exception, while
                            <code>Optional.ofNullable(null)</code> produces
                            an empty Optional.

                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- SUMMARY -->
        <section class="mb-4">

            <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

                <h5 class="fw-bold">
                    Summary
                </h5>

                <p class="mb-0">
                    Optional represents a value that may or may not be
                    available. Important methods include of, ofNullable,
                    empty, isPresent, isEmpty, get, orElse, orElseGet,
                    orElseThrow, ifPresent, ifPresentOrElse, filter, map,
                    flatMap, and or. Optional is especially useful for making
                    potentially absent method results explicit.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>


